// Weapon glows: the 1.12 weapon enchants' glows, sold in the shop (Shop, Enchants tab) for points
// to spend. A glow bought is the whole warband's; each hero wears one (or none), picked on its
// hero sheet (Equipment), on all its weapons at once: the main hand, an off-hand weapon and the
// ranged weapon, never a shield or a held off-hand item. It shows at
// the camp fire and in runs and changes nothing else. docs/game/achievements.md has the rules,
// docs/game/AUTHORING.md "A weapon glow" how to add one. An id is kept in the save once shipped:
// never change one.
//
// enchant: a SpellItemEnchantment.dbc id of the 1.12.1 client whose ItemVisual (field 22) is the
//          glow; each checked (2026-10-27), its ItemVisual and model in the comment.
// needs:   another glow the warband must own first (the damage glows' ladder).
// Prices: 30, Crusader, Unholy and Fiery 50 (the plan's drafts); the damage glows 15, 30, 50 and
// Feedback 30 (in steps of 15, 30 and 50 from 25, 50 and 75).
([
    (
        id: "crusader",
        name: "Crusader",
        icon: "Spell_Holy_GreaterHeal",
        enchant: 1900, // ItemVisual 103, WhiteGlow_Low
        price: 50, // draft
        text: "The white light of the Crusader enchant.",
    ),
    (
